# ⬢ Geo user guide

Every page: [llms.txt](llms.txt), or all in one file: [llms-full.txt](llms-full.txt)

*Measure and draw shapes with the Geo library, from installation to custom shapes.*

Geo measures and draws two-dimensional shapes. This guide is the sample suite for the Markdown importer: each page
exercises some of the Markdown the importer reads. For the classes themselves, read the
[API reference](https://example.com/api/index.html).

## Sections

- [Getting started](guides/getting-started.md): install Geo and measure a first shape.
- [Concepts](guides/concepts/index.md): shapes, units, callouts and pictures.
- [Advanced topics](guides/concepts/advanced/index.md): what a custom shape must do.

## What each page shows

| Page | Markdown it uses |
| --- | --- |
| [Getting started](guides/getting-started.md) | fenced code, task lists, strikethrough, autolinks, a link to a section |
| [Callouts](guides/concepts/alerts.md) | the five GitHub alerts, an explicit heading id, raw HTML |
| [Pictures](guides/concepts/images.md) | a PNG and an SVG image, a download link |
| [Custom shapes](guides/concepts/advanced/custom-shapes.md) | a nested group, links up and across |

The [developer guide](https://example.com/developer/index.html) covers embedding Geo; its
[shapes section](https://example.com/developer/guides/concepts/shapes.html#the-shape-interface) starts with the interface.

---

Next: [Getting started](guides/getting-started.md)
"
`;

exports[`guides-only site snapshots: guides/getting-started.md 1`] = `
"---
title: "Getting started"
description: "Install Geo, then measure your first shape."
kind: "guide"
id: "guide:geo/getting-started"
module: "Geo user guide"
version: "2.1.0"
canonical: "https://docs.example.com/geo/guides/getting-started.html"
---

# ¶ Getting started

[Geo user guide](../index.md) · Every page: [llms.txt](../llms.txt)

*Install Geo, then measure your first shape.*

Geo needs Java 21 or later. ~~Java 17 is supported.~~ Java 17 support ended with 2.0.

## Install

Add the dependency with Gradle:

\`\`\`kotlin
dependencies {
    implementation("com.example:geo:2.1.0")
}
\`\`\`

Or with Maven:

\`\`\`xml
<dependency>
  <groupId>com.example</groupId>
  <artifactId>geo</artifactId>
  <version>2.1.0</version>
</dependency>
\`\`\`

## Measure a shape

\`\`\`java
Shape circle = new Circle(2.0);
System.out.println(Shapes.area(circle));
\`\`\`

\`\`\`text
12.566370614359172
\`\`\`

The result is in the square of the unit you measured in; [Units](concepts/index.md#units) explains which.

## Checklist

- [x] Add the dependency
- [x] Measure a circle
- [ ] Read [the callouts page](concepts/alerts.md#before-you-start)

Questions go to [mailto:geo@example.com](mailto:geo@example.com) or [https://example.com/geo/issues](https://example.com/geo/issues). Back to [the top](getting-started.md#install).

---

Previous: [Geo user guide](../index.md)  
Next: [Concepts](concepts/index.md)
"
`;

exports[`guides-only site snapshots: guides/concepts/alerts.md 1`] = `
"---
title: "Callouts"
description: "The five GitHub alerts, an explicit heading id and raw HTML."
kind: "guide"
id: "guide:geo/concepts/alerts"
module: "Geo user guide"
version: "2.1.0"
canonical: "https://docs.example.com/geo/guides/concepts/alerts.html"
---

# ¶ Callouts

[Geo user guide](../../index.md) › [Concepts](index.md) · Every page: [llms.txt](../../llms.txt)

*The five GitHub alerts, an explicit heading id and raw HTML.*

## Before you start

> [!NOTE]
> Measurements are exact for circles and polygons.

> [!TIP]
> Reuse a \`Shapes.Builder\` to build many shapes.

> [!IMPORTANT]
> Shapes are immutable: every transform returns a new shape.

> [!WARNING]
> A polygon whose edges cross has no defined area.

> [!CAUTION]
> \`Shapes.parse\` reads untrusted text: limit its input size.
>
> It allocates one object per vertex.

## A plain quote

> Geometry is the art of correct reasoning from incorrectly drawn figures.

## Raw HTML

Press Ctrl+C to copy. Water is H2O, and E = mc2.

Area The size of the inside.

---

Back to the [concepts](index.md#shapes).

---

Previous: [Concepts](index.md)  
Next: [Pictures](images.md)
"
`;

